{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Norman nobleman who ruled the County of Tripoli in the 12th century. He was the last ruler of the County of Tripoli of the Norman dynasty and the last Count of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Reign*\n\nRaymond III was born in 1154 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and his wife Gersende of Bari. He succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152. After the death of his father in 1152 Raymond III married his cousin Constance of Antioch in 1153. Raymond III expanded the County of Tripoli's territories and strengthened its economy. He also improved the county's defenses and military strength.\n\n*The Battle of Hattin*\n\nRaymond III played a significant role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the army of Saladin defeated the Kingdom of Jerusalem. Raymond III was present at the battle and led the defense of the County of Tripoli's forces. He managed to escape the battle and flee to Sicily where he was received by King William II of Sicily.\n\n*Exile and Death*\n\nRaymond III spent the rest of his life in exile in Sicily. He died in 1187 in the town of Trapani in Sicily. He was succeeded by Raymond of Châtillon who was a member of Raymond's family but was not of the same bloodline as his predecessors.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0016098171472549438}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001308832288486883}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.16895784437656403}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.802703940891661e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002967870968859643}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -7.068861305015162e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.008241336792707443}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.3622196912765503}, {"token": " Norman", "logprob": -1.3288697004318237}, {"token": " noble", "logprob": -0.915867805480957}, {"token": "man", "logprob": -0.021299